// Story translations · Chapter 18, The Lost Hand (Parts CXII–CXVIII) · 日本語
// Columns: English | Español | Français | Deutsch | Português | 日本語. Empty columns stay in English.
// Keep {g:a|b|c} and {he}/{him}/{his} markers as they are: the game fills them in afterwards.
(window.LOR_STORY = window.LOR_STORY || []).push(
  ["The Lost Hand", "", "", "", "", "失われた手"],
  ["Kline Gerrand", "", "", "", "", "クライン・ジェランド"],
  ["Each Hollow Hand with you can do one thing for you on this job, once. When a favour would help, it turns up as a choice or a button.", "", "", "", "", "一緒にいる虚ろの手の仲間は、この仕事でそれぞれ一度だけ力を貸してくれる。助けになる場面で、選択肢かボタンとして現れる。"],
  ["Part CXII", "", "", "", "", "パートCXII"],
  ["The Empty Hand", "", "", "", "", "空の手"],
  ["It's waiting for you on the roads back, nailed to the door of an inn you've never stopped at before: an iron badge with an open hand on it and a hole through the middle of the palm. Under the nail, a folded note.", "", "", "", "", "帰り道で、一度も立ち寄ったことのない宿の扉に釘で打ちつけられて待っている。手のひらの真ん中に穴の開いた開いた手の鉄の記章だ。釘の下に、たたんだ書き付けがある。"],
  ["We had a job across the Narrow Sea, and it went wrong, and they've got Grell. I wouldn't ask. I'm asking. The den. Come quick. S.", "", "", "", "", "狭き海の向こうで仕事があって、しくじった。グレルが捕まった。頼みたくはない。でも頼む。隠れ家へ。急いで。S"],
  ["Ysolde tells it. A village across the Narrow Sea, on Selvaine, in the jungle they call the Wetwood: Amberlow, a gum-tappers' village, and its headwoman hired the Hollow Hands to steal back the village's deeds. A man called", "", "", "", "", "イゾルデが話す。狭き海の向こう、セルヴェインの、湿り森と呼ばれる密林にある村、樹脂採りの村アンバーロウ。その村長が村の権利証書を盗み返すよう虚ろの手を雇った。証書を持っているのは"],
  ["has them. He used to be a bailiff in the debt courts of Sulmara. Now he's on Selvaine, buying the Wetwood up holding by holding, from people who don't want to sell, and building himself a hold on the falls at Cutwater with a palisade round it.", "", "", "", "", "という男だ。かつてスルマーラの債務法廷の執行吏だった。今はセルヴェインにいて、売りたくない人々から湿り森を一区画ずつ買い上げ、カットウォーターの滝の上に柵で囲った砦を築いている。"],
  ["\"Grell went in by the culvert,\" she says. \"The way we always do. And the culvert was waiting for him. A pit with a cage at the bottom that came up on a rope as soon as he dropped into it. They swung him out on a boom over the falls, and he's hanging there now, with the whole Wetwood watching him.\" She puts a letter on the table. \"This came the day after.\"", "", "", "", "", "「グレルは暗渠から入った」と彼女は言う。「いつものやり方で。そして暗渠が待ち構えてた。底に檻のある穴で、落ちたとたんに綱で引き上げられた。滝の上の張り出し梁に吊り出されて、今もそこにぶら下がってる。湿り森じゅうに見られながら」彼女はテーブルに手紙を置く。「これが次の日に届いた」"],
  ["The letter is in a clerk's round hand, very neat, on thick paper the colour of honey.", "", "", "", "", "手紙は書記の丸い筆跡でとても丁寧に、蜂蜜色の厚い紙に書かれている。"],
  ["To the Hollow Hands, at the sign of the empty hand. I hold one of yours. The cage hangs from a rope and the rope from a counterweight and the counterweight is a cistern under the sky, and the rains come in a week. When the cistern fills, the boom tips. Come and talk to me about what that's worth. Yours in good standing, K. Gerrand, of Cutwater.", "", "", "", "", "空の手の看板のもと、虚ろの手の諸君へ。君たちの一人を預かっている。檻は綱に吊られ、綱は錘に繋がり、錘は空に開いた貯水槽で、一週間後に雨季が来る。貯水槽が満ちれば梁が傾く。それにどれほどの値打ちがあるか、話しに来たまえ。敬具、カットウォーターのK・ジェランド。"],
  ["You cross the Narrow Sea on a gum-trader's ketch out of a Sulmaran creek, four days east with the wind behind you, and the sea goes from grey to green to a brown like strong tea where the Wetwood rivers run out into it. Then there's Selvaine: a wall of trees along the whole horizon, steaming in the sun.", "", "", "", "", "スルマーラの入り江から出る樹脂商人の小型帆船で狭き海を渡る。追い風で東へ四日、海は灰色から緑へ、そして湿り森の川が流れ込むところでは濃い茶のような茶色になる。それからセルヴェインが見える。水平線いっぱいに木々の壁が、陽の中で湯気を立てている。"],
  ["A new continent.", "", "", "", "", "新たな大陸。"],
  ["Selvaine is on your map now, east across the Narrow Sea. The map has grown to fit it.", "", "", "", "", "セルヴェインが地図に載った。狭き海を渡った東だ。地図はそれに合わせて広がった。"],
  ["Brindle Landing is a harbour town built on stilts over the mud of a river mouth, all plank walks and rope bridges and the smell of hot gum. Half the houses have a notice nailed to the door in the same neat clerk's hand:", "", "", "", "", "ブリンドル船着き場は河口の泥の上に杭で建てられた港町で、板の通路と綱の橋ばかりで、熱い樹脂の匂いがする。家の半分の戸口に、同じ丁寧な書記の筆跡の告知が打ちつけてある："],
  ["This holding is the property of K. Gerrand. Rent is due on the first.", "", "", "", "", "この地所はK・ジェランドの所有である。地代は一日に支払うこと。"],
  ["Start asking questions", "", "", "", "", "聞き込みを始める"],
  ["Ammeroth offered the contract again, and you signed.", "", "", "", "", "アメロスがまた契約を差し出し、お前は署名した。"],
  ["Amberlow", "", "", "", "", "アンバーロウ"],
  ["Each day, go to one place. Some places tell you who sold the job; some give you a way in, or a trick for later. You won't get to all of them. When the days are up you name someone, or nobody.", "", "", "", "", "一日に一か所行け。誰が仕事を売ったか教えてくれる場所もあれば、入り方や後で使える手を教えてくれる場所もある。全部は回れない。日数が尽きたら誰かを名指しするか、誰も名指ししない。"],
  ["A clearing of weeping-boles in the Wetwood, every trunk cut and cupped, red gum pooled sticky between the roots, and the rain coming down through the canopy in ropes.", "", "", "", "", "湿り森の泣き幹の空き地。どの幹にも切れ目と杯があり、根のあいだに赤い樹脂がべたべたと溜まり、雨が樹冠から綱のように降り注いでいる。"],
  ["the fence", "", "", "", "", "故買屋"],
  ["Needlewings", "", "", "", "", "針翼鳥"],
  ["While three or more are left, three of them strike each round instead of two, quick as thrown pins.", "", "", "", "", "三羽以上残っているあいだは、毎ラウンド二羽ではなく三羽が、投げたピンのように素早く突いてくる。"],
  ["Thin them fast. Below three they go back to the flowers, which they like better than you.", "", "", "", "", "早く数を減らせ。三羽を切ると花のほうへ戻っていく。お前より花のほうが好きなのだ。"],
  ["Birds of the Wetwood no longer than your finger, with bills like darning needles and wings you can't see, that drink the red gum out of the tappers' cups and anything else that's warm. A cloud of them sounds like a kettle coming to the boil.", "", "", "", "", "指ほどの長さもない湿り森の鳥で、繕い針のような嘴と見えない翼を持ち、採取人の杯の赤い樹脂や、ほかの温かいものなら何でも飲む。群れはやかんが沸く音がする。"],
  ["There's a sound like a kettle coming to the boil, and it's coming from everywhere.", "", "", "", "", "やかんが沸くような音がする。そこらじゅうから。"],
  ["Stilt-cat", "", "", "", "", "竹馬猫"],
  ["It comes down out of the canopy from far off, all at once, legs first.", "", "", "", "", "遠くの樹冠から、脚から先に、一気に降りてくる。"],
  ["Get something over your head: a branch, a roof, a ledge. When it misses it's on the ground, long and awkward: hit it then.", "", "", "", "", "頭上に何かを置け。枝、屋根、岩棚。外したとき地面の上で長くぎこちなくなる。そのときに打て。"],
  ["A jungle cat with legs twice as long as they ought to be, that lives in the high canopy of the Wetwood and hunts by dropping. The tappers wear wicker hats with spikes on top. They say it helps.", "", "", "", "", "あるべき長さの倍の脚を持つ密林の猫で、湿り森の高い樹冠に住み、落ちてきて狩る。採取人たちは天辺に棘のついた籐の帽子をかぶる。効くと言っている。"],
  ["Overhead, a branch you'd taken for a branch unfolds.", "", "", "", "", "頭上で、枝だと思っていた枝が広がる。"],
  ["It lands where you were and folds up like a dropped easel.", "", "", "", "", "さっきまでお前がいたところに着地し、落とした画架のように折り畳まれる。"],
  ["The stilt-cat goes back up into the canopy, leaving a lot of itself behind.", "", "", "", "", "竹馬猫は自分の多くを残して樹冠へ戻っていく。"],
  ["It overshoots and hangs half out of the water, thrashing: advantage on your next swing.", "", "", "", "", "飛び越しすぎて半分水から出てぶら下がり、暴れている：次の一振りは有利。"],
  ["Part CXIII", "", "", "", "", "パートCXIII"],
  ["Four Days Before the Rains", "", "", "", "", "雨季の四日前"],
  ["Corbel Fettle's back room", "", "", "", "", "コーベル・フェトルの奥の部屋"],
  ["the crew's fence in Brindle Landing", "", "", "", "", "ブリンドル船着き場の一味の故買屋"],
  ["The land office", "", "", "", "", "土地事務所"],
  ["Gerrand's ledgers · Investigation", "", "", "", "", "ジェランドの帳簿 · 調査"],
  ["Iddo Mabry's boat", "", "", "", "", "イドー・メイブリーの舟"],
  ["the boatman who rowed the crew upriver", "", "", "", "", "一味を川上へ漕いだ船頭"],
  ["the boatman", "", "", "", "", "船頭"],
  ["the gum-tappers' village, and the headwoman who hired the job", "", "", "", "", "樹脂採りの村と、仕事を依頼した村長"],
  ["The ridge over Cutwater", "", "", "", "", "カットウォーターを見下ろす尾根"],
  ["scout the hold · Perception", "", "", "", "", "砦を偵察する · 知覚"],
  ["The gum-buyers' camp", "", "", "", "", "樹脂買いの野営"],
  ["the people Gerrand sells to", "", "", "", "", "ジェランドが売る相手"],
  ["Gerrand's survey stones", "", "", "", "", "ジェランドの測量石"],
  ["where his men mark out the land they take", "", "", "", "", "彼の手下が奪った土地に印をつける場所"],
  ["Ossel", "", "", "", "", "オッセル"],
  ["the headwoman's son", "", "", "", "", "村長の息子"],
  ["the gum-buyer", "", "", "", "", "樹脂買い"],
  ["Corbel Fettle keeps a chandler's shop on the plank walk, and the chandlery is a front for the back room, and the back room is a front for the cellar, where he buys whatever comes across the Narrow Sea without its papers. He's a little anxious man who owns three cats and is frightened of all of them.", "", "", "", "", "コーベル・フェトルは板の通路で船具屋を営んでいて、船具屋は奥の部屋の隠れ蓑で、奥の部屋は地下室の隠れ蓑だ。そこで狭き海を書類なしで渡ってくるものは何でも買う。猫を三匹飼っていて、三匹とも怖がっている小心な小男だ。"],
  ["\"Somebody sold Gerrand the job, aye,\" he says. \"Not me. I'd never get my money. I heard his yardmen talk: the plan they had was on", "", "", "", "", "「誰かがジェランドに仕事を売ったのは確かだ」と彼は言う。「俺じゃない。金がもらえるはずがない。あいつの庭番どもが話してるのを聞いた。連中が持ってた計画図は"],
  ["gum-paper", "", "", "", "", "樹脂紙"],
  [". The yellow stuff they make up at Amberlow, from the bark. Nobody down here writes on it. It's for prayers.\"", "", "", "", "", "に書いてあった。アンバーロウで樹皮から作る黄色いやつだ。この辺じゃ誰もあれに字なんか書かない。祈りのためのものだ」"],
  ["\"And that gum-buyer, Quillfern, that everybody blames for everything? He was in my cellar all that night, losing at Hollowjack to my wife. He owes her nine silver.\"", "", "", "", "", "「それと、何でもかんでもあいつのせいにされる樹脂買いのクイルファーン？ あの晩はずっと俺の地下室で、うちのかみさんにホロウジャックで負けてたよ。銀貨九枚の借りがある」"],
  ["The land office is the only stone building in Brindle Landing, and it's Gerrand's. A clerk with a pen behind each ear is copying deeds by lamplight, and there are a great many deeds.", "", "", "", "", "土地事務所はブリンドル船着き場で唯一の石造りの建物で、ジェランドのものだ。両耳にペンを挟んだ書記がランプの明かりで証書を写していて、証書はとてもたくさんある。"],
  ["Investigation check (the land office ledgers)", "", "", "", "", "調査判定（土地事務所の帳簿）"],
  ["In the harbour book on the counter, anyone can read the tide-warden's log for the night of the job:", "", "", "", "", "カウンターの港の帳簿で、仕事の夜の潮番の記録は誰でも読める："],
  ["Out at dusk to the reef, back at dawn: I. Mabry, boat, with one passenger, C. Fettle, and his cats.", "", "", "", "", "夕暮れに岩礁へ出て、夜明けに帰着：I・メイブリー、舟、乗客一名、C・フェトルと猫たち。"],
  ["Iddo Mabry and Corbel Fettle spent the night on the reef together, with three cats, a long way from Cutwater.", "", "", "", "", "イドー・メイブリーとコーベル・フェトルは三匹の猫と一緒に、カットウォーターから遠く離れた岩礁で一晩過ごしていた。"],
  ["And in the holdings ledger, in the clerk's round hand:", "", "", "", "", "そして地所台帳に、書記の丸い筆跡で："],
  ["Amberlow, nine holdings, taken as surety on a debt of play, signed O. Ashlowe.", "", "", "", "", "アンバーロウ、九区画、賭けの借金の担保として取得、署名O・アッシュロウ。"],
  ["And a line under it, dated the morning after the job:", "", "", "", "", "そしてその下に、仕事の翌朝の日付で一行："],
  ["Surety discharged. Debt forgiven in full by K. Gerrand.", "", "", "", "", "担保解除。K・ジェランドにより借金全額免除。"],
  ["The holdings ledger is thick as a door and the clerk is watching. You don't get far into it.", "", "", "", "", "地所台帳は扉ほど分厚く、書記が見ている。あまり先まで読めない。"],
  ["Iddo Mabry lives on his boat, a long flat gum-barge with a roof of palm thatch, and he's an old man with arms like rope who only ever says what's needed. \"I rowed them up,\" he says. \"I'd row you. There's a gate on the river side where the falls come down, under the mist. They open it at the change of the watch to let the gum barges out.\"", "", "", "", "", "イドー・メイブリーは舟で暮らしている。椰子の葉葺きの屋根をかけた細長く平たい樹脂運びのはしけで、綱のような腕をした老人で、必要なことしか言わない。「あいつらを漕いで上った」と彼は言う。「あんたも漕いでやる。滝が落ちてくる川側に門がある。霧の下だ。見張りの交代のときに樹脂のはしけを出すために開ける」"],
  ["He spits over the side. \"Night of the job I was on the reef. With Fettle and his cats. Ask the tide-warden.\"", "", "", "", "", "彼は舷側から唾を吐く。「仕事の夜は岩礁にいた。フェトルと猫たちとな。潮番に聞いてみな」"],
  ["Amberlow is a village of round houses up on stilts round a pool the colour of honey, and every tree round it has a cut in the bark with a cup under it, and the cups are full of red gum, and all of it is Gerrand's now. Headwoman", "", "", "", "", "アンバーロウは蜂蜜色の池を囲んで杭の上に建つ丸い家々の村で、周りのどの木にも樹皮に切れ目があってその下に杯があり、杯は赤い樹脂で満ちていて、そのすべてが今はジェランドのものだ。村長の"],
  ["Nennet Ashlowe", "", "", "", "", "ネネット・アッシュロウ"],
  ["is a tall grey woman with gum on her hands to the elbow, and her son", "", "", "", "", "は肘まで手に樹脂をつけた背の高い白髪の女で、息子の"],
  ["is standing behind her in a pair of brand-new boots.", "", "", "", "", "が真新しいブーツを履いて後ろに立っている。"],
  ["\"Nine of our holdings he took,\" Nennet says, \"for a debt. I don't know whose. He wouldn't tell me. When I hired your friends, I told nobody but my own house.\" Behind her Ossel looks at his boots.", "", "", "", "", "「九区画も持っていかれた」とネネットは言う。「借金のかたに。誰の借金かは知らない。教えてくれなかった。あんたの仲間を雇ったとき、話したのは身内だけだよ」後ろでオッセルが自分のブーツを見ている。"],
  ["Insight check (Ossel)", "", "", "", "", "洞察判定（オッセル）"],
  ["Watch him", "", "", "", "", "彼を観察する"],
  ["He's not frightened of you. He's frightened of his mother. And on the post by the door there's his tally-stick, the one every tapper carries with his debts notched in it, and his has been planed smooth.", "", "", "", "", "彼はお前を怖がってはいない。母親を怖がっている。そして戸口の柱に彼の勘定棒が掛かっている。採取人なら誰でも借金を刻んで持ち歩くもので、彼のは削られてつるつるになっている。"],
  ["Before you go, Nennet takes you to the edge of the pool, where the tappers who've been taken up to Cutwater on Gerrand's bond have left their cups upside down on the posts. \"If you get in there,\" she says, \"they're ours. Tell them Amberlow sent you, and they'll know what to do.\"", "", "", "", "", "帰り際、ネネットは池の縁へお前を連れていく。ジェランドの年季で砦へ連れていかれた採取人たちが、柱に杯を伏せて置いていったところだ。「中に入れたら」と彼女は言う。「あの人たちはうちの者だ。アンバーロウから来たと言えば、どうすればいいかわかる」"],
  ["You climb a strangler-fig on the ridge above Cutwater before dawn, with the whole Wetwood steaming below you, and lie in the crook of it all day, drawing.", "", "", "", "", "夜明け前にカットウォーターの上の尾根の絞め殺しの無花果に登り、眼下で湿り森全体が湯気を立てるなか、一日じゅうその股に寝そべって描く。"],
  ["Watch the walls", "", "", "", "", "壁を見張る"],
  ["By dusk you've got it all down: the palisade, the four towers, the yard paved with flags that the yardmen walk round and never across, the counting-house, the gum works with its vats and its bunk-sheds, the kennels, and the boom over the falls.", "", "", "", "", "夕暮れまでにすべて描き取る。柵、四つの塔、庭番たちが周りは歩いても決して横切らない敷石の庭、勘定所、大桶と寝小屋のある樹脂工場、犬小屋、そして滝の上の梁。"],
  ["And the cage. It's turning slowly on its rope in the spray, and there's a big man in it, sitting with his back to the bars and his knees up. Once, at noon, he gets up and spits through the bars into the falls, carefully, as if he's aiming at something. It's Grell.", "", "", "", "", "そして檻。しぶきの中で綱に吊られてゆっくり回っていて、中に大男がいる。格子に背をもたせて膝を立てて座っている。一度、正午に立ち上がり、何かを狙うように慎重に、格子越しに滝へ唾を吐く。グレルだ。"],
  ["You've learned the guards' rounds: once inside, the first lantern that would catch you won't.", "", "", "", "", "見張りの巡回を覚えた：中に入れば、最初に見つかるはずのランタンは見逃してくれる。"],
  ["The gum-buyers' camp is a cluster of tents on the riverbank below the hold, where the barges come down from Cutwater loaded with red gum in wax-sealed jars. The buyers come from all over the Narrow Sea, and they have the look of people who don't ask where things come from.", "", "", "", "", "樹脂買いの野営は砦の下の川岸に集まった天幕で、蝋で封をした壺に赤い樹脂を積んだはしけがカットウォーターから下ってくる。買い手は狭き海じゅうから来ていて、物の出どころを尋ねない人々の顔をしている。"],
  ["Talk prices", "", "", "", "", "値段の話をする"],
  ["You talk prices with a buyer from Rahdaria until he likes you, and then you buy his pass, a little wax seal on a cord, for a jar of nothing. Buyers walk in at the front gate of Cutwater every morning to taste the gum.", "", "", "", "", "ラダリアから来た買い手と気に入られるまで値段の話をし、それから中身のない壺一つで彼の通行証、紐に下げた小さな蝋の封印を買う。買い手は毎朝カットウォーターの正門から入って樹脂を味見する。"],
  ["Out in the Wetwood, where Gerrand's men have marked out new holdings, there are survey stones every hundred paces with his mark on them: a K inside a square. At one of them a yardman has left his kit while he relieves himself in the trees: a surveyor's chain, and a little book.", "", "", "", "", "湿り森の外れ、ジェランドの手下が新しい区画に印をつけたところに、百歩ごとに彼の印のついた測量石がある。四角の中のK。その一つで、庭番が木立で用を足すあいだに道具を置いていっている。測量鎖と小さな帳面だ。"],
  ["Sleight of Hand check (the surveyor's book)", "", "", "", "", "手先の早業判定（測量士の帳面）"],
  ["The book is Gerrand's yard-plan: the flags of the trapwright's yard, numbered, and a few of them inked in. It's not all of them. It's the ones the yardmen have to know so as not to step on them.", "", "", "", "", "帳面はジェランドの庭の図面だ。罠師の庭の敷石に番号が振られ、いくつかがインクで塗られている。全部ではない。庭番が踏まないよう知っておかなければならないものだけだ。"],
  ["He comes back out of the trees buttoning himself up and sees you, and runs.", "", "", "", "", "彼はボタンを留めながら木立から戻ってきてお前を見つけ、走り出す。"],
  ["He's running for Cutwater.", "", "", "", "", "カットウォーターへ走っていく。"],
  ["Where do you go?", "", "", "", "", "どこへ行く？"],
  ["On the last night the gang sits up in a stilt-house on the edge of Brindle Landing, with the rain coming in off the sea and the frogs going like a mill, and puts it together.", "", "", "", "", "最後の夜、一味はブリンドル船着き場の外れの杭上家屋で起きていて、海から雨が吹き込み、蛙が水車のように鳴くなか、話をまとめる。"],
  ["Name nobody", "", "", "", "", "誰も名指ししない"],
  ["go in without knowing", "", "", "", "", "知らないまま入る"],
  ["You go back up to Amberlow in the rain and ask Ossel Ashlowe, in front of his mother, why his tally-stick is smooth.", "", "", "", "", "雨の中アンバーロウへ戻り、母親の前でオッセル・アッシュロウに、なぜ勘定棒がつるつるなのか尋ねる。"],
  ["He tells it all at once, the way a dam goes. Hollowjack in Brindle Landing, a winter of it, nine holdings of his mother's signed away as surety. And then Gerrand's clerk came up the river with an offer: the debt forgiven, every notch of it, for the night and the route of the thieves his mother had hired. \"He said nobody would get hurt,\" Ossel says. \"He said it was just a cage.\"", "", "", "", "", "彼は堰が切れるように一気に話す。ブリンドル船着き場でひと冬続けたホロウジャック、担保として署名して手放した母親の九区画。そこへジェランドの書記が申し出を持って川を上ってきた。借金を刻み目一つ残らず帳消しにする、その代わりに母親が雇った盗賊たちの夜と道筋を教えろ、と。「誰も傷つかないって言ったんだ」とオッセルは言う。「ただの檻だって」"],
  ["Leave him to his mother", "", "", "", "", "母親に任せる"],
  ["Amberlow's own justice", "", "", "", "", "アンバーロウ自身の裁き"],
  ["Make him open the river gate for you", "", "", "", "", "川の門を開けさせる"],
  ["he takes the gum barges out · an easier way in", "", "", "", "", "彼が樹脂のはしけを出す · 入りやすくなる"],
  ["Let him run", "", "", "", "", "逃がしてやる"],
  ["into the Wetwood, before Gerrand hears", "", "", "", "", "ジェランドに知られる前に湿り森へ"],
  ["He goes the same night, with a bundle and no boots, into the trees. Nennet watches him go from the door, and doesn't say anything, and doesn't shut it.", "", "", "", "", "その夜、彼は包みを一つ持ち、ブーツも履かずに木々の中へ去っていく。ネネットは戸口から見送り、何も言わず、扉も閉めない。"],
  ["You go down to the river to have it out with Iddo Mabry, and he hears you out, and spits over the side, and casts off. \"Ask the tide-warden,\" he says, from the middle of the river. Nobody will be rowing you to the river gate now.", "", "", "", "", "イドー・メイブリーと話をつけに川へ降りると、彼は最後まで聞き、舷側から唾を吐き、舫いを解く。「潮番に聞いてみな」と川の真ん中から言う。もう誰も川の門まで漕いでくれない。"],
  ["Corbel Fettle goes white, and then pink, and then he locks his shop with you outside it. Whatever you'd have wanted from his cellar, you won't be getting it.", "", "", "", "", "コーベル・フェトルは青くなり、それから赤くなり、お前を外に締め出して店に鍵をかける。地下室から欲しかったものが何であれ、もう手に入らない。"],
  ["You had what you needed to name the right one.", "", "", "", "", "正しい者を名指しするのに必要なものは揃っていた。"],
  ["Go up to Cutwater", "", "", "", "", "カットウォーターへ上る"],
  ["Guards walk their beats, there and back. Each sees his own square and two ahead (the lit ones); walls and vats block the look, and in a bush you're only seen from right next to it. Move one square, or wait, and then they all take a step. Stand beside a guard who isn't facing you and tap him to take him down (that takes your turn).", "", "", "", "", "見張りは持ち場を行き来する。それぞれ自分のマスと前方二マス（明るいマス）が見える。壁と大桶は視線を遮り、茂みの中なら真横からしか見えない。一マス動くか待つと、全員が一歩進む。こちらを向いていない見張りの隣に立って叩けば倒せる（ターンを使う）。"],
  ["Cutwater's alarm runs from 0 to 6. A failed check, being seen or springing plates raises it. The higher it is, the more yardmen come, and the harder Gerrand is.", "", "", "", "", "カットウォーターの警戒度は0から6。判定の失敗、見つかること、板を作動させることで上がる。高いほど庭番が多く来て、ジェランドも手強くなる。"],
  ["The frogs in the Wetwood all stop at once. Then one of them starts again, on its own, and after a while the others join in, as if it's been forgiven.", "", "", "", "", "湿り森の蛙がいっせいに鳴きやむ。それから一匹がひとりでまた鳴きはじめ、しばらくすると、許されたかのようにほかの蛙も加わる。"],
  ["Ishbel's knives", "", "", "", "", "イシュベルのナイフ"],
  ["The cudgel whistles past your ear.", "", "", "", "", "棍棒が耳元をかすめて唸る。"],
  ["Go in loud", "", "", "", "", "派手に押し入る"],
  ["Sable's whistle", "", "", "", "", "セーブルの口笛"],
  ["Inside the palisade", "", "", "", "", "柵の内側"],
  ["Wait a breath", "", "", "", "", "一息待つ"],
  ["Part CXIV", "", "", "", "", "パートCXIV"],
  ["The Palisade", "", "", "", "", "柵"],
  ["The first of the rain comes the night you go up: not falling so much as standing in the air, warm as breath, so that the whole Wetwood drips and steams and the frogs go quiet one by one.", "", "", "", "", "お前が上る夜、最初の雨が来る。降るというより、息のように温かく宙に立ちこめていて、湿り森じゅうが滴り湯気を立て、蛙が一匹ずつ黙っていく。"],
  ["Up the river to the water-gate", "", "", "", "", "川を上って水門へ"],
  ["Through the culvert", "", "", "", "", "暗渠を通る"],
  ["the way Grell went · Athletics", "", "", "", "", "グレルが通った道 · 運動"],
  ["Over the wall by the canopy", "", "", "", "", "樹冠から壁を越える"],
  ["a rope from a strangler-fig · Acrobatics", "", "", "", "", "絞め殺しの無花果から綱 · 軽業"],
  ["In at the front gate as a gum-buyer", "", "", "", "", "樹脂買いとして正門から入る"],
  ["The culvert comes out of the bottom of the palisade in the south-west corner, a stone mouth older than Cutwater, older than Gerrand, breathing out warm air that smells of gum and rot. Grell went in this way. You can see where the pit was dug: a square of new planking in the floor of it, a little way in, and scratches on the stone where something big went down fighting.", "", "", "", "", "暗渠は柵の南西の隅の下から出ている。カットウォーターより古く、ジェランドより古い石の口で、樹脂と腐敗の匂いのする温かい空気を吐き出している。グレルはここから入った。穴が掘られた場所が見える。少し入ったところの床に新しい板張りの四角があり、石には何か大きなものが抗いながら落ちていった引っかき傷がある。"],
  ["Athletics check (bridging the pit)", "", "", "", "", "運動判定（穴をまたぐ）"],
  ["Brace and climb", "", "", "", "", "突っ張って登る"],
  ["Somewhere above you a little bell is ringing.", "", "", "", "", "頭上のどこかで小さな鈴が鳴っている。"],
  ["Sable does the talking at the gate, as a buyer from Rahdaria with very particular views on the colour of gum, and the gatekeeper is so busy agreeing with her he forgets to look at you at all.", "", "", "", "", "門ではセーブルが、樹脂の色にひどくこだわるラダリアの買い手を演じて話を引き受け、門番は彼女に相槌を打つのに忙しくて、お前のことはまったく見ない。"],
  ["Inside, you let the other buyers go on up to the tasting shed and step sideways into the dark between two gum-stores.", "", "", "", "", "中に入ると、ほかの買い手たちが味見小屋へ上っていくのに任せ、二つの樹脂倉のあいだの暗がりへ横にそれる。"],
  ["Inside the palisade it's dark and close and smells of hot gum, and the yardmen walk their rounds with shuttered lanterns that throw a long thin light ahead of them.", "", "", "", "", "柵の内側は暗く息苦しく、熱い樹脂の匂いがし、庭番たちが前方へ細長い光を投げる覆いつきのランタンを持って巡回している。"],
  ["You give up on the shadows.", "", "", "", "", "物陰に隠れるのをあきらめる。"],
  ["Into the yard", "", "", "", "", "庭へ"],
  ["tick", "", "", "", "", "かち"],
  ["click", "", "", "", "", "かちり"],
  ["The Counting Floor", "", "", "", "", "勘定の床"],
  ["Each flag you've stood on shows how many plates touch it, all eight ways round. You can only step next to where you've already been. Use chalk mode to mark the plates you've worked out. Four sprung plates and the yard wakes up. You never have to guess.", "", "", "", "", "踏んだ敷石には、周囲八方向で接している板の数が表示される。すでに立った場所の隣にしか進めない。白墨モードで割り出した板に印をつけろ。四枚作動させると庭全体が目覚める。当て推量は一度も必要ない。"],
  ["Set four pins (1 to 5) and try them. A", "", "", "", "", "四本のピン（1〜5）を合わせて試せ。"],
  ["is a right height on the right pin; a", "", "", "", "", "は正しいピンの正しい高さ、"],
  ["is a right height on the wrong pin. It doesn't tell you which. Eight tries.", "", "", "", "", "は違うピンの正しい高さだ。どれかは教えてくれない。八回まで。"],
  ["Each flag you stand on shows how many plates touch it, all eight ways round. You can step onto any flag next to one you've stood on. Chalk (✎) the flags you think are plates, so you don't forget. Get to the far row.", "", "", "", "", "立った敷石には、周囲八方向で接している板の数が表示される。立ったことのある敷石の隣ならどこへでも進める。板だと思う敷石には白墨（✎）で印をつけて忘れないようにしろ。向こう端の列にたどり着け。"],
  ["✎ Chalk mode: off", "", "", "", "", "✎ 白墨モード：オフ"],
  ["Run for it", "", "", "", "", "走り抜ける"],
  ["Try the pins", "", "", "", "", "ピンを試す"],
  ["The counting-house lock", "", "", "", "", "勘定所の錠"],
  ["Four brass pins, each set from 1 to 5. Try them, and the lock answers: a", "", "", "", "", "真鍮のピンが四本、それぞれ1から5に合わせる。試すと錠が答える：正しい高さのピン一本ごとに"],
  ["for each pin at the right height, a", "", "", "", "", "、違うピンにある正しい高さ一つごとに"],
  ["for each right height that's on the wrong pin. Eight tries. After the fifth, a needle in the keyhole starts to bite.", "", "", "", "", "。八回まで。五回目を過ぎると、鍵穴の針が噛みはじめる。"],
  ["Force it", "", "", "", "", "こじ開ける"],
  ["Part CXV", "", "", "", "", "パートCXV"],
  ["The Trapwright's Yard", "", "", "", "", "罠師の庭"],
  ["Kline Gerrand doesn't only catch thieves. He sells the means. The yard in the middle of Cutwater is where he tries them: a square of numbered flags in the lamplight, with the trap-makers' prototypes standing round the walls like a sculpture garden. Drop-nets on gantries. A rail of dart-tubes. A deadfall of gum-glued logs. A row of iron jaws in different sizes, labelled.", "", "", "", "", "クライン・ジェランドは盗賊を捕まえるだけではない。その手段も売っている。カットウォーターの真ん中の庭で、それを試すのだ。ランプの明かりの中の番号つきの敷石の四角で、周りの壁には罠職人の試作品が彫刻庭園のように並んでいる。台の上の落とし網。吹き矢筒の手すり。樹脂で固めた丸太の落とし罠。大きさ順にラベルを貼った鉄の顎の列。"],
  ["On a post at the edge of the flags there's a painted board, very neat:", "", "", "", "", "敷石の縁の柱に、とても丁寧に塗った板が掛かっている："],
  ["THE COUNTING FLOOR. Each flag will tell you how many of its neighbours would rather you didn't. K.G.", "", "", "", "", "勘定の床。どの敷石も、隣のいくつがお前を歓迎していないか教えてくれる。K・G"],
  ["Gerrand's yard-book: two of the plates are already chalked for you.", "", "", "", "", "ジェランドの庭の帳面：板のうち二枚はすでに白墨で印がついている。"],
  ["The yard's traps make a lot of noise for traps.", "", "", "", "", "庭の罠は罠にしては騒がしい。"],
  ["They come out of the kennel-yard and the gum-stores all at once, yardmen with catchpoles and shields and two big catch-dogs on chains, and they form up at the edge of the flags, and none of them will step on one.", "", "", "", "", "犬小屋の庭と樹脂倉から、捕縛棒と盾を持った庭番と鎖に繋いだ大きな捕獲犬が二頭、いっせいに出てきて敷石の縁に整列するが、誰も一枚も踏もうとしない。"],
  ["You break away through the gantries, and they don't follow you off the flags.", "", "", "", "", "台のあいだを抜けて逃げ出す。彼らは敷石の外までは追ってこない。"],
  ["The counting-house stands in the middle of the hold, built out of the blocks of the old ruin: a squat stone box with one door, one lit window, and on the door a lock with four brass pins in a row, like teeth.", "", "", "", "", "勘定所は砦の真ん中に、古い廃墟の石材で建てられている。扉が一つ、灯りのともった窓が一つのずんぐりした石の箱で、扉には歯のように並んだ四本の真鍮のピンの錠がある。"],
  ["Ask Ysolde for a drop of acid", "", "", "", "", "イゾルデに酸を一滴頼む"],
  ["one pin eaten clean · her favour", "", "", "", "", "ピン一本をきれいに溶かす · 彼女の手助け"],
  ["Do it yourself", "", "", "", "", "自分でやる"],
  ["Ysolde unstoppers a little bottle with her teeth, and puts one drop into the keyhole, and the lock hisses like a cat.", "", "", "", "", "イゾルデが歯で小瓶の栓を抜き、鍵穴に一滴垂らすと、錠が猫のようにしゅうっと鳴る。"],
  ["You put your shoulder into the door, and it doesn't care, and inside the little bell goes on ringing. You get in through the window in the end, cut and swearing, and the deeds are there in their pigeonholes, hundreds of them, but there's a lamp on the floor now, kicked over, and the gum-paper is going up like kindling.", "", "", "", "", "扉に肩を入れるが、扉は意に介さず、中では小さな鈴が鳴り続ける。最後には切り傷を作り悪態をつきながら窓から入る。証書は何百と仕切り棚に収まっているが、床にはランプが蹴り倒されていて、樹脂紙が焚きつけのように燃え上がっていく。"],
  ["Smoke out of the counting-house window.", "", "", "", "", "勘定所の窓から煙。"],
  ["Dexterity check (out of the fire)", "", "", "", "", "敏捷判定（火から逃れる）"],
  ["Grab what you can", "", "", "", "", "掴めるものを掴む"],
  ["You come out through the smoke with the box from the desk under your arm, Amberlow's nine, and the board of bond-tallies. Everything else burns.", "", "", "", "", "机の上の箱、アンバーロウの九区画分と、年季札の板を小脇に抱えて煙の中から出てくる。ほかはすべて燃える。"],
  ["You come out with the board of bond-tallies and your eyebrows, and nothing else. Every deed in Cutwater burns behind you, including the ones that were somebody's before they were his.", "", "", "", "", "年季札の板と眉毛だけを持って出てくる。ほかには何もない。カットウォーターのすべての証書が背後で燃える。彼のものになる前は誰かのものだった証書も。"],
  ["Go round to the gum works", "", "", "", "", "樹脂工場へ回る"],
  ["Let him go", "", "", "", "", "逃がす"],
  ["The gum works by night", "", "", "", "", "夜の樹脂工場"],
  ["Part CXVI", "", "", "", "", "パートCXVI"],
  ["The Gum Works", "", "", "", "", "樹脂工場"],
  ["The gum works are at the back of the hold, under the old ruin's top terrace: four great iron vats of red gum simmering over charcoal pits, and the smell of it thick enough to chew. The tappers sleep in bunk-sheds between the vats, chained to a running rail by one ankle each. There are thirty-one of them. Each one has a tag on the chain with a number on it, and the number is what they owe.", "", "", "", "", "樹脂工場は砦の奥、古い廃墟の最上段の下にある。炭火の穴の上で赤い樹脂を煮る大きな鉄の大桶が四つ、噛めそうなほど濃い匂い。採取人たちは大桶のあいだの寝小屋で、片足首ずつ通し棒に鎖で繋がれて眠る。三十一人いる。それぞれの鎖に番号の札がついていて、番号は借りの額だ。"],
  ["You'll have to get across the works to the sheds first, between the vats, and the yardmen are walking the rounds there too, with their lanterns shuttered against the gum fumes.", "", "", "", "", "まず大桶のあいだを抜けて工場を渡り、寝小屋まで行かなければならない。そこでも庭番たちが樹脂の煙を避けて覆いをしたランタンを持って巡回している。"],
  ["A lantern finds you between the vats.", "", "", "", "", "大桶のあいだでランタンに見つかる。"],
  ["\"Bond-tappers,\" says a woman on the end bunk, without opening her eyes. \"We sold him the land, and then we sold him the work, and then we owed him the rent on our own houses.\" She opens her eyes. \"You're not a yardman.\"", "", "", "", "", "「年季採取人さ」と端の寝台の女が目も開けずに言う。「あいつに土地を売って、それから働きを売って、それから自分の家の地代を借りた」彼女は目を開ける。「あんた、庭番じゃないね」"],
  ["You tell her Amberlow sent you. She sits up. Up and down the shed, in the dark, other people sit up too.", "", "", "", "", "アンバーロウから来たと告げる。彼女が起き上がる。暗い小屋のあちこちで、ほかの者たちも起き上がる。"],
  ["Free them now", "", "", "", "", "今すぐ解放する"],
  ["Tell them to wait", "", "", "", "", "待つように言う"],
  ["you'll come back for them once Grell's out", "", "", "", "", "グレルを出したら戻ってくる"],
  ["You read the numbers off the board of bond-tallies, and snap each stick across your knee, and the woman on the end bunk takes the keys off the hook where they've always been, a yard out of reach, and the chains come off one at a time.", "", "", "", "", "年季札の板から番号を読み上げ、札を一本ずつ膝で折る。端の寝台の女が、いつも一ヤード手の届かないところにあった鉤から鍵を取り、鎖が一つずつ外れていく。"],
  ["When the last chain's off, the tappers don't run. They pick up their tapping knives, which are hooked and very sharp, and stand behind you.", "", "", "", "", "最後の鎖が外れても、採取人たちは逃げない。鉤形でとても鋭い採取用のナイフを拾い上げ、お前の後ろに立つ。"],
  ["\"Wait,\" says the woman on the end bunk. \"We've been doing that.\" She lies down again, and turns her face to the wall.", "", "", "", "", "「待つ、ね」と端の寝台の女が言う。「ずっとそうしてきたよ」彼女はまた横になり、壁のほうを向く。"],
  ["Then a voice from the top of the vat-stairs, a big cheerful voice with a whistle in it: \"There you are.\" It's", "", "", "", "", "そのとき大桶の階段の上から声がする。口笛の混じった大きく陽気な声だ。「そこにいたか」"],
  ["Hessary Ruckley", "", "", "", "", "ヘサリー・ラックリー"],
  [", Gerrand's yard-boss: a huge man in a gum-stiffened apron, with a bailiff's brass-headed staff and a row of iron keys at his belt for every chain in the place.", "", "", "", "", "、ジェランドの庭番頭だ。樹脂でこわばった前掛けをした巨漢で、真鍮頭の執行吏の杖を持ち、ベルトにはここのすべての鎖の鉄の鍵が並んでいる。"],
  ["\"Mister Gerrand said you'd come in by the culvert,\" Ruckley says. \"He was very disappointed when you didn't.\" He leans on the rail. \"You'll be wanting the falls path. It's behind me.\"", "", "", "", "", "「ジェランドさんは、あんたが暗渠から来ると言ってた」とラックリーは言う。「来なかったんで、えらくがっかりしてたよ」彼は手すりにもたれる。「滝の道に用があるんだろ。俺の後ろだ」"],
  ["Behind you, thirty-one tappers with hooked knives come out of the bunk-sheds, and Ruckley's whistle stops halfway through.", "", "", "", "", "背後で、鉤形のナイフを持った三十一人の採取人が寝小屋から出てきて、ラックリーの口笛が途中で止まる。"],
  ["Ruckley's brass-headed staff rings off your guard.", "", "", "", "", "ラックリーの真鍮頭の杖がお前の守りに当たって鳴る。"],
  ["You get past them up the vat-stairs and onto the falls path, with Ruckley bellowing behind you.", "", "", "", "", "彼らをすり抜けて大桶の階段を上り、滝の道へ出る。背後でラックリーががなり立てている。"],
  ["Ruckley goes down at the foot of the vat-stairs, and sits there in the gum with his staff across his knees, laughing, holding his ribs.", "", "", "", "", "ラックリーは大桶の階段の下に倒れ、杖を膝に渡して樹脂の中に座り込み、肋を押さえて笑っている。"],
  ["Chain him to his own rail", "", "", "", "", "自分の通し棒に鎖で繋ぐ"],
  ["Tip him into the gum", "", "", "", "", "樹脂の中へ落とす"],
  ["the gum sets hard as amber", "", "", "", "", "樹脂は琥珀のように固まる"],
  ["he'll run, or he'll run to Gerrand", "", "", "", "", "逃げるか、ジェランドのところへ走るか"],
  ["He picks himself up and touches his forehead to you, very polite, and goes off up the falls path ahead of you, at a run.", "", "", "", "", "彼は起き上がってとても丁寧に額に手をやって挨拶し、お前の先に立って滝の道を走っていく。"],
  ["He's gone to tell Gerrand.", "", "", "", "", "ジェランドに知らせに行った。"],
  ["Up the falls path", "", "", "", "", "滝の道を上る"],
  ["Cutwater", "", "", "", "", "カットウォーター"],
  ["Say no", "", "", "", "", "断る"],
  ["The sluices", "", "", "", "", "水門"],
  ["Pour one cistern into another and it runs until the first is empty or the second is full. Get exactly the measure asked for into the counterweight. There's always a way, and a shortest one.", "", "", "", "", "ある貯水槽から別の貯水槽へ注ぐと、最初のものが空になるか次のものが満ちるまで流れる。錘にちょうど求められた量を入れろ。必ず方法があり、最短のものがある。"],
  ["the counterweight", "", "", "", "", "錘"],
  ["Every few rounds Gerrand backs to the balustrade and takes hold of a yard-cord. Cut it before his turn, or Evade, or take what comes. Crossing the Counting Floor cleanly makes the cords easier to cut.", "", "", "", "", "数ラウンドごとにジェランドは手すりまで下がって庭の綱を一本掴む。彼の番の前に切るか、回避するか、来るものを受けろ。勘定の床をきれいに渡っていれば、綱は切りやすくなる。"],
  ["Swim", "", "", "", "", "泳ぐ"],
  ["The boom swings the cage in to the ledge when", "", "", "", "", "梁が檻を岩棚へ振り寄せるのは"],
  ["holds exactly", "", "", "", "", "がちょうど"],
  ["Part CXVII", "", "", "", "", "パートCXVII"],
  ["The falls path comes out on the top terrace of the old ruin, on a shelf of black rock with the whole river going over the edge beside it in a roar you can feel in your teeth. The boom reaches out from the shelf over the drop, a great tarred beam on a pivot, with a rope down from the end of it to the cage. Behind the pivot, the counterweight: a stone cistern open to the sky, with the rain pocking its surface, already three-quarters full.", "", "", "", "", "滝の道は古い廃墟の最上段、黒い岩の棚に出る。その横で川全体が、歯で感じるほどの轟きとともに縁から落ちている。梁は棚から落差の上へ突き出ている。軸に載った大きなタール塗りの梁で、先端から綱が檻まで垂れている。軸の後ろには錘。空に開いた石の貯水槽で、雨が水面をたたき、もう四分の三まで満ちている。"],
  ["And between you and the boom, at a little table under an oiled-silk awning, with a ledger open in front of him and a lamp and a pot of tea, is", "", "", "", "", "そしてお前と梁のあいだ、油を引いた絹の日除けの下の小さなテーブルに、帳簿を開き、ランプと茶のポットを前に座っているのが"],
  ["He's a neat, narrow man in a bailiff's black coat buttoned to the throat, with grey hair cut very short and a clerk's ink-stained middle finger. He has a long catchpole leaning on the table beside him, the kind with a spring-hook at the end for taking hold of a man by the neck. He finishes the line he's writing before he looks up.", "", "", "", "", "だ。喉元までボタンを留めた執行吏の黒い上着の、きちんとした細身の男で、白髪をとても短く刈り、中指は書記らしくインクで汚れている。テーブルの横に長い捕縛棒が立てかけてある。先にばね仕掛けの鉤がついていて、人の首を捕らえるためのものだ。彼は書きかけの行を書き終えてから顔を上げる。"],
  ["\"Everybody's land is somebody's,\" he says. \"I just write it down first. Sit, if you like. I've an offer.\"", "", "", "", "", "「誰の土地も誰かのものだ」と彼は言う。「わたしは先に書き留めるだけだ。よければ座りたまえ。申し出がある」"],
  ["\"Walk away and leave me the man in the cage, and I'll write you fifteen hundred gold on the Sulmaran bank. He's a thief. He came to rob me. I'm only asking what the law would.\"", "", "", "", "", "「立ち去って、檻の男をわたしに残していきたまえ。そうすればスルマーラの銀行宛てに金貨千五百枚を書いてやろう。あれは盗賊だ。わたしの物を盗みに来た。法が求めることを求めているだけだよ」"],
  ["and take Grell out of that cage", "", "", "", "", "、そしてグレルをあの檻から出す"],
  ["Tell him his counting-house is on fire", "", "", "", "", "勘定所が燃えていると告げる"],
  ["it is · no roll", "", "", "", "", "本当に燃えている · 判定なし"],
  ["Take his offer", "", "", "", "", "申し出を受ける"],
  ["You take the pen. Gerrand watches you sign, and blots it, and puts it away in the ledger.", "", "", "", "", "ペンを取る。ジェランドはお前が署名するのを見て、吸い取り紙を当て、帳簿にしまう。"],
  ["Gerrand sighs, and stands, and picks up his catchpole. \"I did say it was an offer for you,\" he says. \"I didn't say it was an offer for them.\"", "", "", "", "", "ジェランドはため息をつき、立ち上がり、捕縛棒を手に取る。「申し出は君へのものだと言った」と彼は言う。「彼らへのものだとは言っていない」"],
  ["You took Kline Gerrand's 1,500 gold. The Hollow Hands will remember. So will Grell.", "", "", "", "", "お前はクライン・ジェランドの金貨1,500枚を受け取った。虚ろの手は覚えている。グレルも。"],
  ["The spring-hook snaps shut on the rain where your neck was.", "", "", "", "", "ばね仕掛けの鉤が、さっきまでお前の首があった雨の中で閉じる。"],
  ["Gerrand steps back, and touches the place, and looks at the blood on his fingers as if it's a figure that doesn't add up.", "", "", "", "", "ジェランドは一歩下がってその場所に触れ、指についた血を、合わない数字でも見るように見つめる。"],
  ["The tappers from the gum works come up the falls path behind you with their hooked knives, and stop at the edge of the shelf, and watch. This is yours. They'll make sure nobody else comes up.", "", "", "", "", "樹脂工場の採取人たちが鉤形のナイフを持って滝の道を上ってきて、棚の縁で止まって見ている。これはお前の戦いだ。ほかに誰も上ってこないよう見張ってくれる。"],
  ["Gerrand gives ground to the old balustrade, where a dozen yard-cords come up out of the rock and run off into the ruin, and puts his free hand on one of them.", "", "", "", "", "ジェランドは古い手すりまで後退する。そこでは十数本の庭の綱が岩から出て廃墟の中へ走っていて、彼は空いた手を一本に置く。"],
  ["He's going to pull a cord. Cut it before he does, or get out of the way.", "", "", "", "", "綱を引くつもりだ。その前に切るか、どけ。"],
  ["Cut the cord", "", "", "", "", "綱を切る"],
  ["Dexterity check (cut the cord)", "", "", "", "", "敏捷判定（綱を切る）"],
  ["You cut it through an inch from his hand. Somewhere in the ruin, something that was going to fall doesn't.", "", "", "", "", "彼の手から一インチのところで切り落とす。廃墟のどこかで、落ちるはずだった何かが落ちない。"],
  ["The blade bounces off the gum-stiff cord.", "", "", "", "", "刃が樹脂でこわばった綱に弾かれる。"],
  ["Kline Gerrand goes down on one knee on the wet rock, and the catchpole goes over the edge and into the falls, and he watches it go. Then he does the only fast thing you ever see him do: he pulls his little knife and cuts the boom's brake-line.", "", "", "", "", "クライン・ジェランドは濡れた岩に片膝をつき、捕縛棒が縁を越えて滝へ落ち、彼はそれを見送る。それから、お前が見た唯一の素早い動きをする。小さなナイフを抜いて、梁の制動索を切るのだ。"],
  ["The boom swings. The cage drops a yard on its rope and stops with a jerk that throws Grell into the bars, and the counterweight cistern sloshes, and the beam begins, very slowly, to tip toward the river. \"Arithmetic,\" Gerrand says, and sits down in the rain.", "", "", "", "", "梁が揺れる。檻が綱で一ヤード落ちてがくんと止まり、グレルが格子に叩きつけられ、錘の貯水槽が波打ち、梁がとてもゆっくりと川のほうへ傾きはじめる。「算術だ」とジェランドは言い、雨の中に座り込む。"],
  ["The rope gives, and the cage drops into the spray, and without thinking about it at all you go off the ledge after it.", "", "", "", "", "綱が切れ、檻がしぶきの中へ落ち、何も考えずにお前もそれを追って岩棚から飛び込む。"],
  ["Athletics check (the plunge pool)", "", "", "", "", "運動判定（滝壺）"],
  ["You get the cage door open on the bottom of the plunge pool, in the white dark, by feel, and you get Grell out of it, and somehow you get him up. He's alive. His right leg isn't right, and won't be again.", "", "", "", "", "白い闇の中、手探りで滝壺の底の檻の扉を開け、グレルを引き出し、どうにか引き上げる。生きている。右脚がおかしく、二度と元には戻らないだろう。"],
  ["Grell looks at you for a long time. Then he takes the lockpick out from behind his ear, where it's been all along, and picks his teeth with it, and says, in a voice like a door that hasn't been opened in a year: \"Took your time.\"", "", "", "", "", "グレルは長いことお前を見る。それからずっとそこにあった耳の後ろの錠前破りを取り出し、それで歯をほじり、一年開けられていなかった扉のような声で言う。「遅かったな」"],
  ["Down from the falls", "", "", "", "", "滝から降りる"],
  ["You freed the bond-tappers of the gum works.", "", "", "", "", "お前は樹脂工場の年季採取人たちを解放した。"],
  ["Turn", "", "", "", "", "回す"],
  ["Gerrand", "", "", "", "", "ジェランド"],
  ["Selvaine", "", "", "", "", "セルヴェイン"],
  ["the rain", "", "", "", "", "雨"],
  ["the counting-house", "", "", "", "", "勘定所"],
  ["the falls", "", "", "", "", "滝"],
  ["Then", "", "", "", "", "それから"],
  ["the map.", "", "", "", "", "地図。"],
  ["the cage", "", "", "", "", "檻"],
  ["the culvert", "", "", "", "", "暗渠"],
  ["Grell's lockpick.", "", "", "", "", "グレルの錠前破り。"],
  ["plates touch it", "", "", "", "", "枚の板に接している"],
  ["Pour", "", "", "", "", "注ぐ"],
  ["It was", "", "", "", "", "それは"],
  ["Try", "", "", "", "", "試す"],
  ["Vat", "", "", "", "", "大桶"],
  ["Point", "", "", "", "", "指す"],
  ["the river gate", "", "", "", "", "川の門"],
  ["river gate", "", "", "", "", "川の門"],
  ["with you:", "", "", "", "", "一緒にいる仲間："],
  ["· costs your turn", "", "", "", "", "· ターンを使う"],
  ["Dexterity DC", "", "", "", "", "敏捷DC"],
  ["the front gate", "", "", "", "", "正門"],
  ["front gate", "", "", "", "", "正門"],
  ["Butt", "", "", "", "", "雨桶"],
  ["taken down", "", "", "", "", "倒した"],
  ["Get to", "", "", "", "", "目指す："],
  ["the gum works", "", "", "", "", "樹脂工場"],
  ["the canopy wall", "", "", "", "", "樹冠側の壁"],
  ["the trapwright's yard", "", "", "", "", "罠師の庭"],
  ["A hand-inked plan of Cutwater: a square palisade of sharpened stakes with a watchtower at each corner, a front gate to the south, a river gate on the east wall by the waterfall, a culvert in the south-west, a grid of pressure plates in the yard, a stone counting-house in the middle, gum vats and bunk-sheds to the north-west, kennels, and a boom over the falls with a cage hanging from it.", "", "", "", "", "手書きのカットウォーターの図面：四隅に見張り塔のある尖った杭の四角い柵、南に正門、東壁の滝のそばに川の門、南西に暗渠、庭には圧力板の格子、真ん中に石の勘定所、北西に樹脂の大桶と寝小屋、犬小屋、そして滝の上に檻を吊った梁。"],
  ["gum vat", "", "", "", "", "樹脂の大桶"],
  ["Cutwater, as you've drawn it", "", "", "", "", "お前が描いたカットウォーター"],
  ["the yard gate", "", "", "", "", "庭の門"],
  ["the falls path", "", "", "", "", "滝の道"],
  ["(⛩). Tap a square next to you to move, or wait. Then every guard takes a step along his beat. A guard sees his own square and two ahead (the lit ones); walls and vats block the look, and in a bush (♣) you can only be seen from right next to it. Stand beside a guard who isn't facing you and take him down.", "", "", "", "", "（⛩）。隣のマスを叩いて動くか、待て。すると見張りが全員持ち場に沿って一歩進む。見張りは自分のマスと前方二マス（明るいマス）が見える。壁と大桶は視線を遮り、茂み（♣）の中なら真横からしか見えない。こちらを向いていない見張りの隣に立って倒せ。"],
  ["The night's going grey at the edges. Somebody is bound to look your way soon.", "", "", "", "", "夜の縁が白みはじめている。そろそろ誰かがこちらを見るだろう。"],
  ["A lantern swings across you, and you go still as a post, and the guard looks right through you. (Your scouting bought you that once.)", "", "", "", "", "ランタンの光がお前を横切り、柱のようにじっとしていると、見張りはお前を素通りして見る。（偵察のおかげで一度だけ）"],
  ["A lantern stops on you. Somebody shouts.", "", "", "", "", "ランタンがお前の上で止まる。誰かが叫ぶ。"],
  ["You come up behind him, and he goes down without a sound.", "", "", "", "", "後ろから近づくと、彼は音もなく倒れる。"],
  ["He's facing you. You can't take him down from the front.", "", "", "", "", "こちらを向いている。正面からは倒せない。"],
  ["He's too far to reach.", "", "", "", "", "遠すぎて届かない。"],
  ["You're through, and nobody saw a thing. (", "", "", "", "", "抜けた。誰にも見られていない。（"],
  ["taken down)", "", "", "", "", "人倒した）"],
  ["Ishbel needs a guard in a straight line, two squares off at most.", "", "", "", "", "イシュベルには、二マス以内の一直線上にいる見張りが必要だ。"],
  ["Ishbel's knife goes past your ear, and the guard sits down and doesn't get up.", "", "", "", "", "イシュベルのナイフが耳元を過ぎ、見張りは座り込んで二度と立たない。"],
  ["Somewhere off to the left Sable whistles like a nightbird with a grievance, and every guard stops to look the wrong way. (2 turns)", "", "", "", "", "左のほうでセーブルが不満げな夜鳥のように口笛を吹き、見張りが全員足を止めて違うほうを見る。（2ターン）"],
  ["You stop sneaking.", "", "", "", "", "こそこそするのをやめる。"],
  ["a guard, down", "", "", "", "", "見張り、倒れた"],
  ["a guard, facing", "", "", "", "", "見張り、向いている方向"],
  [", in a lantern's look", "", "", "", "", "、ランタンの視線の中"],
  ["· they're looking the wrong way", "", "", "", "", "· 違うほうを見ている"],
  ["✎ Chalk mode:", "", "", "", "", "✎ 白墨モード："],
  ["You stop counting and run, and the floor does what floors here do.", "", "", "", "", "数えるのをやめて走ると、床はここの床がすることをする。"],
  ["You've chalked that one. Rub the chalk off first if you're sure.", "", "", "", "", "そこには白墨で印をつけてある。確信があるなら先に白墨を消せ。"],
  ["That's too far. Step next to it first.", "", "", "", "", "遠すぎる。まず隣に行け。"],
  ["Click. Something in the yard wall answers it.", "", "", "", "", "かちり。庭の壁の何かがそれに応える。"],
  ["You're across, with", "", "", "", "", "渡りきった。背後で"],
  ["sprung behind you.", "", "", "", "", "枚が作動した。"],
  ["You're across, and not one plate has moved.", "", "", "", "", "渡りきった。一枚の板も動いていない。"],
  ["The fourth plate goes, and the whole yard wakes up at once.", "", "", "", "", "四枚目の板が作動し、庭全体がいっせいに目覚める。"],
  ["a sprung plate", "", "", "", "", "作動した板"],
  ["a flag you've stood on:", "", "", "", "", "立ったことのある敷石："],
  ["a flag you've chalked", "", "", "", "", "白墨で印をつけた敷石"],
  ["an unknown flag", "", "", "", "", "未知の敷石"],
  ["on the far row", "", "", "", "", "向こう端の列"],
  ["sprung · 4 and the yard wakes", "", "", "", "", "作動 · 4で庭が目覚める"],
  ["plates sprung · 4 and the yard wakes", "", "", "", "", "枚作動 · 4で庭が目覚める"],
  ["Ysolde's acid has eaten one pin clean: it's set, and marked ✓.", "", "", "", "", "イゾルデの酸がピン一本をきれいに溶かした。合わせてあり、✓の印がついている。"],
  ["Raise pin", "", "", "", "", "ピンを上げる"],
  ["Lower pin", "", "", "", "", "ピンを下げる"],
  ["Four clicks, and the bolt goes back like a sigh. (", "", "", "", "", "かちりと四回、閂がため息のように引っ込む。（"],
  ["The eighth try, and the lock seizes solid. Somewhere inside, a little bell rings.", "", "", "", "", "八回目で錠が固く噛み合って動かなくなる。中のどこかで小さな鈴が鳴る。"],
  ["You put your shoulder to it.", "", "", "", "", "肩を当てる。"],
  ["· the needle's awake", "", "", "", "", "· 針が目覚めている"],
  ["the gum vat", "", "", "", "", "樹脂の大桶"],
  ["the rain-butt", "", "", "", "", "雨桶"],
  ["measures. Open a sluice to pour one cistern into another: it runs until the first is empty or the second is full. There's nowhere else for the water to go. You have", "", "", "", "", "の量が必要だ。水門を開けて貯水槽から貯水槽へ注げ：最初のものが空になるか次のものが満ちるまで流れる。水のほかの行き場はない。綱が切れるまでに注げるのは"],
  ["pours before the rope gives.", "", "", "", "", "回だ。"],
  ["The boom groans and swings, and the cage comes in over the ledge and bumps down on the rock. (", "", "", "", "", "梁が唸って揺れ、檻が岩棚の上に入ってきて岩の上にどすんと降りる。（"],
  ["The rope gives.", "", "", "", "", "綱が切れる。"],
  ["· the counterweight needs", "", "", "", "", "· 錘に必要なのは"],
  ["The den under the dunes is quieter than you remember. Sable is at the long table with a map held down by four knives. Ysolde is grinding something in a mortar too hard.", "", "", "", "", "砂丘の下の隠れ家は記憶より静かだ。セーブルは長いテーブルについていて、地図を四本のナイフで押さえている。イゾルデは乳鉢で何かを強すぎる力ですり潰している。"],
  ["Tobbin is in the corner shuffling a deck of cards, and he doesn't look up when you come in, which is how you know he's frightened.", "", "", "", "", "トビンは隅でカードを切っていて、お前が入ってきても顔を上げない。それで怯えているとわかる。"],
  ["Grell's chair is empty, and his tooth-pick, a long thin lockpick worn bright, is on the table in front of it.", "", "", "", "", "グレルの椅子は空で、その前のテーブルに彼の楊枝、擦り減って光る長く細い錠前破りが置いてある。"],
  ["You owe him a hand. You know which one. Cutwater, on Selvaine. If you've any shame left come to the den, and don't expect a drink. Y.", "", "", "", "", "あんたは彼に手一本分の借りがある。どっちの手かわかってるはず。セルヴェインのカットウォーター。恥がまだ残ってるなら隠れ家へ来て。酒は期待しないで。Y"],
  ["The lamp at the top of the den steps goes out as you come down them, the way it always does now. Ysolde is waiting at the bottom with her arms folded and acid-stained gloves on. Sable isn't there. \"She won't be in a room with you,\" Ysolde says. \"She sent me. That's how bad it is.\"", "", "", "", "", "お前が隠れ家の階段を降りると、上のランプが消える。今ではいつもそうだ。イゾルデが腕を組み、酸の染みた手袋をして下で待っている。セーブルはいない。「あんたと同じ部屋にいたくないって」とイゾルデは言う。「わたしをよこした。それくらいひどいってこと」"],
  ["You turned down a job of ours once, and gave us back a waterskin. We need somebody now who isn't one of us and isn't scared of a lock. The den. S.", "", "", "", "", "あんたは一度わたしたちの仕事を断って、水袋を返してくれた。今、仲間じゃなくて錠を怖がらない誰かが要る。隠れ家へ。S"],
  ["The den under the dunes takes a while to find without a token. Sable lets you in herself. She looks older, and tired, and she doesn't make a joke, which you've never seen. Ysolde is at the long table with a map held down by four knives.", "", "", "", "", "しるしがないと砂丘の下の隠れ家はなかなか見つからない。セーブルが自分で入れてくれる。老けて疲れて見え、冗談も言わない。そんな彼女は見たことがない。イゾルデは長いテーブルについていて、地図を四本のナイフで押さえている。"],
  ["Ishbel comes down the steps behind you, and stops, and looks at Grell's empty chair for a long time. \"He always said he'd be the one hauling the rope,\" she says. \"Never the one on it.\"", "", "", "", "", "イシュベルがお前の後から階段を降りてきて立ち止まり、グレルの空の椅子を長いこと見つめる。「綱を引く側になるっていつも言ってた」と彼女は言う。「吊られる側じゃなくて」"],
  ["\"Somebody sold him the job,\" Ysolde says. \"He knew the route, the night and the man. One of the people we used over there.\" She looks at", "", "", "", "", "「誰かがあいつに仕事を売ったんだ」とイゾルデは言う。「道筋も、夜も、人も知ってた。向こうで使った誰かだよ」彼女は"],
  ["you, for a long moment, and then away.", "", "", "", "", "お前を長いこと見て、それから目をそらす。"],
  ["Tobbin, and then away, and Tobbin's hands stop on the cards.", "", "", "", "", "トビンを見て、それから目をそらし、トビンの手がカードの上で止まる。"],
  [". Each can do you one favour on this job:", "", "", "", "", "。この仕事で、それぞれ一度ずつ手を貸してくれる："],
  [". You'll see them when they'd help.", "", "", "", "", "。役に立つときに現れる。"],
  ["Corbel Fettle", "", "", "", "", "コーベル・フェトル"],
  ["Iddo Mabry", "", "", "", "", "イドー・メイブリー"],
  ["Ossel Ashlowe", "", "", "", "", "オッセル・アッシュロウ"],
  ["he's done it before", "", "", "", "", "前にもやったことがある"],
  ["Pellan Quillfern", "", "", "", "", "ペラン・クイルファーン"],
  ["\"And your boy,\" he says, nodding at Tobbin, \"was in my cellar all that night, losing at Hollowjack to my wife till sun-up. He owes her nine silver. Tell him she's counting.\"", "", "", "", "", "「それと、あんたのとこの若いのは」と彼はトビンに顎をしゃくって言う。「あの晩はずっと俺の地下室で、日の出までうちのかみさんにホロウジャックで負けてた。銀貨九枚の借りがある。かみさんが数えてるって伝えといてくれ」"],
  ["He's a nervous young man in new boots, and that's all you can tell.", "", "", "", "", "新しいブーツを履いた神経質な若者で、わかるのはそれだけだ。"],
  ["A painting of a walled hold at night in a jungle: three stone terraces of an old ruin above a waterfall, ringed by a palisade of sharpened trunks, four watchtowers with lanterns, smoke rising from gum vats, a stone counting-house in the middle with one lit window, and a boom reaching out over the falls with a cage hanging from it.", "", "", "", "", "密林の夜の、壁に囲まれた砦の絵：滝の上の古い廃墟の三段の石の段丘を、尖らせた幹の柵が囲み、ランタンを灯した見張り塔が四つ、樹脂の大桶から煙が上がり、真ん中に灯りのともった窓が一つある石の勘定所、そして滝の上に檻を吊った梁が突き出ている。"],
  ["Cutwater, from the ridge", "", "", "", "", "尾根から見たカットウォーター"],
  ["Perception check (the guard rounds)", "", "", "", "", "知覚判定（見張りの巡回）"],
  ["Cutwater, as you drew it from the ridge", "", "", "", "", "尾根から描いたカットウォーター"],
  ["Tobbin knows a few of them. He's been down here every night since the job, it turns out, drinking, and asking who sold it. He looks like he hasn't slept.", "", "", "", "", "トビンは何人か知り合いがいる。聞けば、仕事の後は毎晩ここに降りてきて、飲みながら誰が売ったのか尋ね回っていたらしい。眠っていないような顔だ。"],
  ["Deception check (passing as a buyer)", "", "", "", "", "欺瞞判定（買い手になりすます）"],
  ["The buyers close up like clams. One of them goes up the hill to the hold in a hurry.", "", "", "", "", "買い手たちは貝のように口を閉ざす。一人が急いで丘を砦へ上っていく。"],
  ["Somebody will tell Cutwater there are strangers asking.", "", "", "", "", "誰かがカットウォーターに、よそ者が嗅ぎ回っていると告げるだろう。"],
  ["The rains come in a week, Gerrand said, and the gum-traders in Brindle Landing agree: they can see them, a grey wall out at sea. You've got four days to find out who sold the job and how to get in, and then you'll have to go, ready or not.", "", "", "", "", "雨季は一週間後に来るとジェランドは言い、ブリンドル船着き場の樹脂商人たちも同意する。沖に灰色の壁として見えるのだ。誰が仕事を売ったかとどう入るかを突き止めるのに四日あり、それが過ぎたら、準備ができていてもいなくても行かなければならない。"],
  ["Sable works the plank walks for you while you're busy, which buys you a fifth.", "", "", "", "", "お前が忙しいあいだにセーブルが板の通路を回ってくれて、五日目が手に入る。"],
  ["What you know:", "", "", "", "", "わかっていること："],
  ["not much.", "", "", "", "", "たいしたことはない。"],
  ["Nennet Ashlowe looks at her son for a long time. Then she takes his new boots off him, one and then the other, and throws them in the honey-coloured pool, and sends him to sit on the tappers' bench with an empty cup until she's decided what he's worth.", "", "", "", "", "ネネット・アッシュロウは長いこと息子を見つめる。それから新しいブーツを片方ずつ脱がせて蜂蜜色の池に投げ込み、彼がどれほどの値打ちか決めるまで、空の杯を持たせて採取人の長椅子に座らせる。"],
  ["Ossel drives the gum barges for the hold, it turns out; that was the job Gerrand gave him. Tomorrow night at the change of the watch he'll leave the river gate's bar off. He swears it on his mother. His mother says that's not worth much, and he'd better do it anyway.", "", "", "", "", "聞けば、オッセルは砦の樹脂のはしけを動かしているのだ。それがジェランドから与えられた仕事だった。明日の夜、見張りの交代のときに川の門の閂を外しておくという。母親にかけて誓う。母親はそんなものにたいした値打ちはないと言い、それでもやるんだよと言う。"],
  ["Everybody turns and looks at Tobbin, because everybody already was. He puts the cards down. \"Corbel's wife,\" he says, very quietly. \"Ask Corbel's wife where I was.\"", "", "", "", "", "みんながトビンのほうを向く。最初からみんな見ていたのだ。彼はカードを置く。「コーベルのかみさんに」とごく静かに言う。「俺がどこにいたか、コーベルのかみさんに聞いてくれ」"],
  ["You already know where he was. You say it anyway.", "", "", "", "", "彼がどこにいたかはもう知っている。それでも言う。"],
  ["He gets up and puts his coat on, and goes out into the rain, and he doesn't come back. Sable sits looking at the door for a long time.", "", "", "", "", "彼は立ち上がって上着を着て、雨の中へ出ていき、戻ってこない。セーブルは長いこと扉を見つめて座っている。"],
  ["Pellan Quillfern laughs in your face, and pays Corbel's wife her nine silver in front of you, and asks if there's anybody else you'd like to blame. Word gets round the camp. Nobody's selling you a buyer's pass now.", "", "", "", "", "ペラン・クイルファーンはお前を笑い飛ばし、お前の目の前でコーベルのかみさんに銀貨九枚を払い、ほかに責めたい奴はいるかと訊く。噂が野営に広まる。もう誰もお前に買い手の通行証を売ってくれない。"],
  ["You go in without a name. Whoever sold the job is still out there, and they'll still be selling.", "", "", "", "", "名前なしで入る。仕事を売った者はまだどこかにいて、まだ売り続けるだろう。"],
  ["the plan Gerrand had was on Amberlow gum-paper", "", "", "", "", "ジェランドの計画図はアンバーロウの樹脂紙に書かれていた"],
  ["Tobbin was in Corbel's cellar all night", "", "", "", "", "トビンは一晩じゅうコーベルの地下室にいた"],
  ["Pellan Quillfern was in Corbel's cellar all night", "", "", "", "", "ペラン・クイルファーンは一晩じゅうコーベルの地下室にいた"],
  ["Iddo Mabry and Corbel Fettle were on the reef all night", "", "", "", "", "イドー・メイブリーとコーベル・フェトルは一晩じゅう岩礁にいた"],
  ["O. Ashlowe's debt was forgiven the morning after the job", "", "", "", "", "O・アッシュロウの借金は仕事の翌朝に免除された"],
  ["Iddo says he was on the reef with Fettle", "", "", "", "", "イドーはフェトルと岩礁にいたと言っている"],
  ["Ossel's tally-stick has been planed smooth", "", "", "", "", "オッセルの勘定棒は削られてつるつるになっている"],
  ["Cutwater: which way in?", "", "", "", "", "カットウォーター：どこから入る？"],
  ["Ossel's left the bar off", "", "", "", "", "オッセルが閂を外しておいた"],
  ["Iddo's boat · Stealth", "", "", "", "", "イドーの舟 · 隠密"],
  ["· under the falls' mist", "", "", "", "", "· 滝の霧の下"],
  ["· Tobbin knows a side tunnel", "", "", "", "", "· トビンが脇の抜け道を知っている"],
  ["· Threadfang's line", "", "", "", "", "· スレッドファングの綱"],
  ["the buyer's pass · Deception", "", "", "", "", "買い手の通行証 · 欺瞞"],
  ["· Sable talks", "", "", "", "", "· セーブルが話す"],
  ["Iddo Mabry, or Ossel on a gum barge, it doesn't matter which; the river gate swings open at the change of the watch with the bar off, the way Ossel swore it would, and you're inside with the spray of the falls in your face before anybody's turned round.", "", "", "", "", "イドー・メイブリーでも、樹脂のはしけのオッセルでも、どちらでも構わない。オッセルが誓ったとおり、見張りの交代のときに閂の外れた川の門が開き、誰かが振り向く前に、滝のしぶきを顔に受けながらお前は中にいる。"],
  ["Iddo rows you up under the mist of the falls without a word, the oars wrapped in sacking. The river gate opens at the change of the watch to let the gum barges out.", "", "", "", "", "イドーは袋布でオールを包み、ひと言も言わずに滝の霧の下へ漕ぎ上ってくれる。川の門は見張りの交代のときに樹脂のはしけを出すために開く。"],
  ["Stealth check (in past the barges)", "", "", "", "", "隠密判定（はしけの横を抜ける）"],
  ["A bargeman sees you go over the side.", "", "", "", "", "はしけ乗りがお前が舷側を越えるのを見る。"],
  ["Tobbin crouches, and puts his ear to the wall, and knocks twice, and grins for the first time since you met him in the den. \"It's hollow,\" he says. \"Old drain, under the new one. They built over it.\" He goes first, on his belly, and you follow, and you come up through a grate in the yard with nothing sprung at all.", "", "", "", "", "トビンがしゃがんで壁に耳を当て、二回叩き、隠れ家で会ってから初めてにやりと笑う。「空洞だ」と彼は言う。「新しい排水路の下に古い排水路がある。上から建てたんだ」彼が先に腹ばいで進み、お前が続き、何一つ作動させずに庭の格子から出る。"],
  ["You put your back against one wall and your boots against the other, and go across above the planking like a chimney-sweep, and come down past it into the dark.", "", "", "", "", "片方の壁に背を、もう片方にブーツを突っ張り、煙突掃除人のように板張りの上を渡り、その先の闇へ降りる。"],
  ["Your boot slips onto the planking. It drops, and you catch the edge, and the spikes under it find your legs.", "", "", "", "", "ブーツが板張りに滑る。板が落ち、お前は縁を掴むが、その下の棘が脚を捕らえる。"],
  ["There's a strangler-fig outside the north-west tower with a limb that reaches almost to the stakes. Almost.", "", "", "", "", "北西の塔の外に、杭にほとんど届く枝を持つ絞め殺しの無花果がある。ほとんど。"],
  ["Acrobatics check (a rope over the palisade)", "", "", "", "", "軽業判定（柵越しの綱）"],
  ["You throw a line round the next limb out and swing, and let go at the top of it, and land on the walkway behind the stakes as softly as a cat landing on a cushion it doesn't approve of.", "", "", "", "", "次の枝に綱を投げかけて振り、頂点で手を放し、気に入らないクッションに着地する猫のようにそっと杭の裏の通路に降りる。"],
  ["You come down short, on the stakes, and roll off them and into a gum-shed roof.", "", "", "", "", "届かずに杭の上に落ち、転がり落ちて樹脂小屋の屋根に落ちる。"],
  ["The roof is loud.", "", "", "", "", "屋根がうるさい。"],
  ["Deception check (the buyer's pass)", "", "", "", "", "欺瞞判定（買い手の通行証）"],
  ["Show the seal", "", "", "", "", "封印を見せる"],
  ["The gatekeeper lets you in, and then sends a boy running.", "", "", "", "", "門番は通してくれ、それから少年を走らせる。"],
  ["A yardman's whistle, then another.", "", "", "", "", "庭番の口笛、それからもう一つ。"],
  ["Cutwater yardmen", "", "", "", "", "カットウォーターの庭番"],
  ["A yardman goes down in the red mud.", "", "", "", "", "庭番が一人、赤い泥の中に倒れる。"],
  ["You come out at the gate to the yard without a single lantern having found you, and behind you", "", "", "", "", "ランタン一つにも見つからずに庭の門に出る。背後では"],
  ["asleep in the gum where you left them.", "", "", "", "", "が、置いてきた樹脂の中で眠っている。"],
  ["the rounds go on, round and round, with nobody in them.", "", "", "", "", "巡回は誰もいないまま、ぐるぐると続いている。"],
  ["Each plate that went fired something: darts out of the rail, a net that only half drops, a log that misses.", "", "", "", "", "作動した板はそれぞれ何かを放った。手すりからの吹き矢、半分しか落ちない網、外れる丸太。"],
  ["The kennel-master", "", "", "", "", "犬小屋番"],
  ["the trap gantries", "", "", "", "", "罠の台"],
  ["The kennel-master's catchpole rings off your guard.", "", "", "", "", "犬小屋番の捕縛棒がお前の守りに当たって鳴る。"],
  ["The needle in the keyhole bit you", "", "", "", "", "鍵穴の針に噛まれた"],
  [". Your fingers are going numb.", "", "", "", "", "。指が痺れてきた。"],
  ["Inside, the counting-house is one room, very tidy, lined with pigeonholes, and every pigeonhole has a deed in it, rolled and tied with red tape. There are hundreds. Amberlow's nine are in a box of their own on the desk, waiting to be filed. And under them, in a different hand, older, there's one you weren't expecting:", "", "", "", "", "勘定所の中は一部屋で、とても整頓されていて、仕切り棚が並び、どの棚にも巻いて赤い紐で縛った証書が入っている。何百とある。アンバーロウの九区画分は、整理されるのを待って机の上の専用の箱にある。そしてその下に、別の、もっと古い筆跡で、思いもよらない一枚がある："],
  ["the holding of the dunes above the den of the empty hand, in the Burning Sands, by purchase from the Magistrate's estate.", "", "", "", "", "燃える砂漠、空の手の隠れ家の上の砂丘の地所。判事の遺産より購入。"],
  ["He's been buying the ground the Hollow Hands sleep under. You take the lot: the box, the deed to the den, and the bond-tallies of every tapper in the gum works, hung on a board by the door like keys.", "", "", "", "", "虚ろの手が眠る地面の下を買い取っていたのだ。全部いただく。箱も、隠れ家の証書も、そして扉のそばの板に鍵のように掛けられた、樹脂工場のすべての採取人の年季札も。"],
  ["you've got their bond-tallies ·", "", "", "", "", "年季札がある ·"],
  ["pick thirty-one locks ·", "", "", "", "", "三十一の錠を開ける ·"],
  ["the hold will hear", "", "", "", "", "砦に聞こえる"],
  ["· Amberlow's sign: they'll fight", "", "", "", "", "· アンバーロウのしるし：彼らは戦う"],
  ["You work down the rail, lock by lock, with", "", "", "", "", "通し棒に沿って錠を一つずつ開けていく。"],
  ["Ysolde's acid smoking in the worst of them", "", "", "", "", "いちばん厄介なものにはイゾルデの酸が煙を上げ"],
  ["a bent nail and a lot of patience", "", "", "", "", "曲がった釘とたっぷりの根気で"],
  [". It takes too long.", "", "", "", "", "。時間がかかりすぎる。"],
  ["Somebody hears the chains.", "", "", "", "", "誰かが鎖の音を聞く。"],
  ["When the last chain's off, they go out over the back wall into the Wetwood in their bare feet, silent, and are gone.", "", "", "", "", "最後の鎖が外れると、彼らは裸足で裏の壁を越え、音もなく湿り森へ消えていく。"],
  ["the gum vats", "", "", "", "", "樹脂の大桶"],
  ["Ruckley's yardmen", "", "", "", "", "ラックリーの庭番"],
  ["the tappers will decide about him", "", "", "", "", "採取人たちが彼のことを決める"],
  ["when they're free", "", "", "", "", "自由になったら"],
  ["You put his own ankle-chain on him, the one at the end of the rail, and hang the key on the hook a yard out of reach. \"Fair,\" Ruckley says, and lies back on the bunk, and laughs till he coughs.", "", "", "", "", "通し棒の端にある彼自身の足首の鎖を彼にかけ、鍵を一ヤード手の届かない鉤に掛ける。「公平だ」とラックリーは言い、寝台に仰向けになり、咳き込むまで笑う。"],
  ["He goes into the nearest vat backwards, with a sound like a boot pulled out of mud, and the gum closes over him. When it sets, he'll be there for a thousand years, a big surprised man in amber, still holding his staff.", "", "", "", "", "彼はぬかるみからブーツを引き抜くような音を立てて後ろ向きにいちばん近い大桶に落ち、樹脂がその上で閉じる。固まれば、彼はそこに千年いることになる。琥珀の中の驚いた大男として、杖を握ったまま。"],
  ["Grell is in the cage. He stands up when he sees you", "", "", "", "", "グレルは檻の中にいる。お前を見ると立ち上がる"],
  [". The hook where his left hand was clacks on the bars. His burned face doesn't change.", "", "", "", "", "。左手があったところの鉤が格子に当たってかちりと鳴る。焼けた顔は変わらない。"],
  [", slowly, and puts his face to the bars, and nods once, the way he nodded on the road the day you met.", "", "", "", "", "。ゆっくりと、格子に顔をつけ、お前と出会った日の道でうなずいたように、一度うなずく。"],
  ["\"The Warden's tenant,\" he says. He has a pleasant voice, a little dry, like a man reading out a will. \"You came in by", "", "", "", "", "「番人の借家人か」と彼は言う。感じのいい声で、少し乾いていて、遺言を読み上げる男のようだ。「入ってきたのは"],
  ["the river gate. I'll have words with Ossel.", "", "", "", "", "川の門か。オッセルとは話をしなければ。"],
  ["the culvert after all. I'm touched.", "", "", "", "", "結局、暗渠か。感激したよ。"],
  ["the canopy. Nobody's done that. I'll need a taller fence.", "", "", "", "", "樹冠からか。誰もやったことがない。もっと高い柵が要るな。"],
  ["my front door, as a customer. I respect that.", "", "", "", "", "客として正面からか。敬意を表するよ。"],
  ["\"You've got my deeds in that box, I expect. Including the one for the dunes over the Hollow Hands' den. Keep that one. Keep it, and walk away, and leave me the man in the cage, and I'll write you fifteen hundred gold on the Sulmaran bank besides. The Hands can pay rent to you instead of me. You'd be kinder about it. Everybody wins but him.\" He nods at the cage.", "", "", "", "", "「その箱にわたしの証書が入っているんだろう。虚ろの手の隠れ家の上の砂丘の分も含めて。それは取っておきたまえ。取っておいて立ち去り、檻の男はわたしに残していけ。そうすればスルマーラの銀行宛てに金貨千五百枚も書いてやろう。手の連中はわたしの代わりに君に地代を払えばいい。君のほうが優しいだろう。彼以外は皆得をする」彼は檻に顎をしゃくる。"],
  ["Deception · he'll look", "", "", "", "", "欺瞞 · 彼は振り向く"],
  ["and the den's deed", "", "", "", "", "と隠れ家の証書"],
  ["· leave Grell to the rains", "", "", "", "", "· グレルを雨に任せる"],
  ["Grell sits back down in his cage without a word.", "", "", "", "", "グレルは何も言わずに檻の中に座り直す。"],
  ["Ysolde makes a sound behind you like something tearing.", "", "", "", "", "背後でイゾルデが、何かが裂けるような音を立てる。"],
  ["goes past you at a run, for the boom.", "", "", "", "", "が駆け抜けて梁へ向かう。"],
  ["goes on falling.", "", "", "", "", "は落ち続ける。"],
  ["Deception check (fire in the counting-house)", "", "", "", "", "欺瞞判定（勘定所が燃えている）"],
  ["He looks. It's only for a breath, over his shoulder, down at the counting-house roof", "", "", "", "", "彼は振り向く。肩越しに、勘定所の屋根を見下ろすのはほんの一息だけ"],
  ["with the smoke coming out of it", "", "", "", "", "、そこから煙が出ている"],
  [", but it's a breath, and you're across the shelf before he's turned back.", "", "", "", "", "。だが一息は一息で、彼が向き直る前にお前は棚を渡っている。"],
  ["He doesn't look. \"I'd smell it,\" he says. \"I've a very good nose for my own property.\"", "", "", "", "", "彼は振り向かない。「匂いでわかる」と彼は言う。「自分の財産には鼻が利くんだ」"],
  ["\"No,\" he says, as if he's writing it down. \"Well. I did ask.\" He closes the ledger, and stands, and picks up his catchpole, and walks out from under the awning into the rain.", "", "", "", "", "「断る、か」と彼は書き留めるように言う。「まあ。訊きはした」帳簿を閉じ、立ち上がり、捕縛棒を取り、日除けの下から雨の中へ歩み出る。"],
  ["the drop-net", "", "", "", "", "落とし網"],
  ["A weighted net comes down out of the dark above the shelf, and he hauls you across the rock in it.", "", "", "", "", "棚の上の闇から重りつきの網が落ちてきて、彼が網ごとお前を岩の上で引きずる。"],
  ["the dart rail", "", "", "", "", "吹き矢の手すり"],
  ["A rail of dart-tubes along the old balustrade coughs, all at once, and a dozen little gum-tipped darts find you.", "", "", "", "", "古い手すりに沿った吹き矢筒がいっせいに咳き込み、樹脂を塗った小さな矢が十数本お前に刺さる。"],
  ["the deadfall", "", "", "", "", "落とし罠"],
  ["A gum-glued log comes down on its chains from the ruin above like the end of the world.", "", "", "", "", "樹脂で固めた丸太が上の廃墟から鎖ごと、世界の終わりのように落ちてくる。"],
  ["the jaws", "", "", "", "", "鉄の顎"],
  ["Iron jaws come up out of the rock under your boot, and he holds the cord taut while you get them off.", "", "", "", "", "ブーツの下の岩から鉄の顎が上がってきて、お前がそれを外すあいだ彼は綱をぴんと張っている。"],
  ["The catchpole's spring-hook takes you by the collar and slams you into the rock.", "", "", "", "", "捕縛棒のばね鉤がお前の襟を捕らえ、岩に叩きつける。"],
  ["· you counted the floor", "", "", "", "", "· 床を数えておいた"],
  ["He pulls the cord, and you're already moving.", "", "", "", "", "彼が綱を引く。お前はもう動いている。"],
  ["goes off where you were.", "", "", "", "", "がお前のいたところで作動する。"],
  ["He pulls the cord.", "", "", "", "", "彼が綱を引く。"],
  ["You pull the pin out of the cage door, and it swings open, and Grell climbs out onto the rock, stiff as a man of seventy, and stands up straight.", "", "", "", "", "檻の扉のピンを抜くと扉が開き、グレルが七十の男のようにこわばって岩の上へ這い出し、まっすぐに立つ。"],
  ["The falls hit you like a building coming down.", "", "", "", "", "滝が建物の崩れ落ちるようにお前に叩きつける。"],
  ["Grell looks at you for a long time, with the rain running off his burned face. He holds up the hook. Then he holds out his right hand, the one he's got, and waits to see if you'll take it.", "", "", "", "", "グレルは焼けた顔から雨を滴らせながら長いことお前を見る。鉤を掲げる。それから右手、残っているほうの手を差し出し、お前が握るかどうか待つ。"],
  ["the one he's got", "", "", "", "", "残っているほうの手"],
  ["He doesn't say anything else to you. He's seen you sign. He goes past you to", "", "", "", "", "彼はそれ以上お前に何も言わない。お前が署名するのを見たのだ。お前の横を通り過ぎて"],
  [", and doesn't look back.", "", "", "", "", "のもとへ行き、振り返らない。"],
  ["What the Land Remembers", "", "", "", "", "土地が覚えていること"],
  ["The rains come in properly at dawn, a grey roaring wall of them, and Cutwater stands in the middle of the Wetwood with its gates open and its lanterns out and nobody on the walls.", "", "", "", "", "夜明けに雨季が本格的に来る。灰色の轟く雨の壁だ。カットウォーターは湿り森の真ん中で門を開け放ち、ランタンを消し、壁に誰もいないまま立っている。"],
  ["You go back down to the gum works first, as you promised. The tappers are waiting, chained, exactly where you left them. You break the chains one at a time. Nobody thanks you. They didn't think you'd come.", "", "", "", "", "約束どおり、まず樹脂工場へ降りる。採取人たちは鎖に繋がれたまま、置いてきたところでちょうど待っている。鎖を一つずつ壊す。誰も礼を言わない。来るとは思っていなかったのだ。"],
  ["Kline Gerrand is sitting on the shelf above the falls where you left him, with his ledger open on his knee and the rain running off his short grey hair, making notes. \"I should have bought the rain,\" he says.", "", "", "", "", "クライン・ジェランドは置いてきた滝の上の棚に座ったまま、膝の上に帳簿を開き、短い白髪から雨を垂らしながら書き込みをしている。「雨を買っておくべきだった」と彼は言う。"],
  ["Give him to Amberlow", "", "", "", "", "アンバーロウに引き渡す"],
  ["the tappers' justice · a bond, a cup and a knife", "", "", "", "", "採取人の裁き · 年季と杯とナイフ"],
  ["Take him down to the harbour-reeve at Brindle Landing", "", "", "", "", "ブリンドル船着き場の港長のところへ連れていく"],
  ["the law · he'll buy his way out, maybe", "", "", "", "", "法の裁き · 金で抜け出すかもしれない"],
  ["Let Grell decide", "", "", "", "", "グレルに決めさせる"],
  ["it's his cage", "", "", "", "", "彼の檻だ"],
  ["Put him over the falls", "", "", "", "", "滝に落とす"],
  ["where his catchpole went", "", "", "", "", "彼の捕縛棒が行ったところへ"],
  ["Nennet Ashlowe comes up from Amberlow in the rain with a cup and a tapping-knife and a tally-stick with no notches in it. She gives them to Gerrand. \"Rent's due on the first,\" she says. He looks at the stick for a long time. Then he writes it down.", "", "", "", "", "ネネット・アッシュロウが雨の中アンバーロウから上ってくる。杯と採取用のナイフと、刻み目のない勘定棒を持って。それらをジェランドに渡す。「地代は一日に払うんだよ」と彼女は言う。彼は長いこと棒を見つめる。それから書き留める。"],
  ["The harbour-reeve of Brindle Landing is very pleased to see Kline Gerrand in irons, and very respectful, and asks after his health. You get the feeling the irons are a formality. Still: they're on.", "", "", "", "", "ブリンドル船着き場の港長はクライン・ジェランドが鉄枷をはめられているのを見てとても喜び、とても丁重で、彼の健康を気遣う。鉄枷は形だけのものだという気がする。それでも、はめられてはいる。"],
  ["Grell looks at Gerrand for a while. Then he picks him up by the coat, one-handed, carries him into the cage, and shuts the door, and leaves the key on the ledge a yard out of reach. \"Rains,\" Grell says. He doesn't say whether he means the cistern will fill. Gerrand doesn't ask.", "", "", "", "", "グレルはしばらくジェランドを見る。それから片手で上着ごと持ち上げて檻に運び込み、扉を閉め、鍵を一ヤード手の届かない岩棚に置く。「雨季だ」とグレルは言う。貯水槽が満ちるという意味なのかは言わない。ジェランドも訊かない。"],
  ["He doesn't fight it. He closes the ledger first, and holds it out for you to take, and goes over the edge after his catchpole without another word, very neat about it, the way he did everything.", "", "", "", "", "彼は抗わない。まず帳簿を閉じ、受け取れと差し出し、ひと言もなく捕縛棒を追って縁を越えていく。何事もそうしてきたように、とても几帳面に。"],
  ["That leaves the box of deeds", "", "", "", "", "残るのは証書の箱だ"],
  [": Amberlow's nine, all the others that weren't burned, and the one for the dunes over the den.", "", "", "", "", "：アンバーロウの九区画分、燃えなかったほかのすべて、そして隠れ家の上の砂丘の分。"],
  [": Amberlow's nine, all you saved from the fire.", "", "", "", "", "：アンバーロウの九区画分、火から救えたのはそれだけ。"],
  ["Give every holding back", "", "", "", "", "すべての地所を返す"],
  ["to whoever's name was on it before his", "", "", "", "", "彼の前に名前があった者へ"],
  ["Give them back, but keep the den's deed", "", "", "", "", "返すが、隠れ家の証書は取っておく"],
  ["the ground over the Hollow Hands is yours · rent from the den", "", "", "", "", "虚ろの手の上の地面はお前のもの · 隠れ家から地代"],
  ["Burn the lot", "", "", "", "", "すべて燃やす"],
  ["nobody owns the Wetwood, then", "", "", "", "", "なら、湿り森は誰のものでもない"],
  ["It takes Nennet Ashlowe three days to read the names out in the square at Amberlow, holding by holding, and by the end of it the whole of the Wetwood's come up the river to listen.", "", "", "", "", "ネネット・アッシュロウがアンバーロウの広場で一区画ずつ名前を読み上げるのに三日かかり、終わる頃には湿り森じゅうが川を上って聞きに来ている。"],
  ["You give back every holding in the Wetwood, holding by holding, and put the den's deed inside your coat. The Hollow Hands have a landlord now.", "", "", "", "", "湿り森のすべての地所を一区画ずつ返し、隠れ家の証書を上着の内にしまう。虚ろの手には今や家主がいる。"],
  ["Sable thinks it's the funniest thing she's ever heard, and then she stops laughing, and looks at you.", "", "", "", "", "セーブルはこれまで聞いたいちばん面白い話だと思い、それから笑うのをやめてお前を見る。"],
  ["Ysolde looks at the deed, and at you, and doesn't say anything.", "", "", "", "", "イゾルデは証書を見て、お前を見て、何も言わない。"],
  ["You burn them in the yard, every one, on the Counting Floor. The plates go off in the heat one at a time, all night, like slow fireworks, and the tappers stand round and watch and don't say whether it was right.", "", "", "", "", "庭の勘定の床で、一枚残らず燃やす。熱で板が一晩じゅう一枚ずつ、ゆっくりした花火のように作動し、採取人たちは周りに立って眺め、それが正しかったかどうかは言わない。"],
  ["Grell goes home with", "", "", "", "", "グレルは"],
  [". You go home on your own, with Gerrand's gold.", "", "", "", "", "と帰っていく。お前はジェランドの金を持って一人で帰る。"],
  ["Take his hand", "", "", "", "", "手を握る"],
  ["You take it. His grip is the same as it was on the road. \"Square,\" Grell says. It's the first thing he's said to you since the desert, and he says it like he's been holding it in his mouth for years.", "", "", "", "", "握る。握り方は道で会ったときと同じだ。「貸し借りなしだ」とグレルは言う。砂漠以来、初めてお前にかけた言葉で、何年も口の中にためていたかのように言う。"],
  ["Then he presses the lockpick into your palm: the long thin one he picks his teeth with, worn bright.", "", "", "", "", "それから錠前破りをお前の手のひらに押しつける。歯をほじる、擦り減って光る長く細いやつだ。"],
  ["He lowers his hand, and nods, as if that's fair, and goes.", "", "", "", "", "彼は手を下ろし、それが公平だというようにうなずき、去っていく。"],
  ["At the Landing, waiting for the ketch, Grell sits down on the plank walk next to you with his bad", "", "", "", "", "船着き場で小型帆船を待つあいだ、グレルはお前の隣の板の通路に座り、悪い"],
  ["leg out straight", "", "", "", "", "脚をまっすぐ伸ばす"],
  ["back against a post", "", "", "", "", "背中を柱にもたせる"],
  [", and after a long time he takes the lockpick from behind his ear and holds it out to you. The long thin one he picks his teeth with, worn bright.", "", "", "", "", "。長いことたってから、耳の後ろから錠前破りを取ってお前に差し出す。歯をほじる、擦り減って光る長く細いやつだ。"],
  ["\"Spare,\" he says. You've never seen him without it. You don't think he has a spare.", "", "", "", "", "「予備だ」と彼は言う。彼がそれなしでいるのは見たことがない。予備を持っているとは思えない。"],
  ["Ossel Ashlowe is on the tappers' bench at Amberlow, with an empty cup, when you go by on the way down. He doesn't look up. His mother brings him his supper, and stands over him while he eats it.", "", "", "", "", "帰りがけに通ると、オッセル・アッシュロウは空の杯を持ってアンバーロウの採取人の長椅子に座っている。顔を上げない。母親が夕食を運んできて、彼が食べるあいだそばに立っている。"],
  ["Nobody has seen Tobbin since the night in the stilt-house. Corbel Fettle's wife says somebody left nine silver on her doorstep.", "", "", "", "", "杭上家屋の夜以来、トビンを見た者はいない。コーベル・フェトルのかみさんは、誰かが戸口に銀貨九枚を置いていったと言う。"],
  ["Sable splits what was in Gerrand's strongbox with you, even shares, the way the Hands do:", "", "", "", "", "セーブルはジェランドの金庫の中身を、手のやり方どおり、きっちり山分けしてくれる："],
  ["Amberlow pays the crew's fee to you, in red gum and silver:", "", "", "", "", "アンバーロウが一味の報酬を、赤い樹脂と銀貨でお前に払ってくれる："],
  ["Gerrand's Tenant", "", "", "", "", "ジェランドの借家人"],
  ["Hand of the Hollow Hands", "", "", "", "", "虚ろの手の一員"],
  ["is on the roads back now: Brindle Landing, Amberlow, the Wetwood's beasts, its board and a hidden thing. Your title is", "", "", "", "", "が今は帰り道にある：ブリンドル船着き場、アンバーロウ、湿り森の獣、その盤、そして隠されたもの。お前の称号は"],
);
